sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Mon as Azure Monitor<br/>(alert)
    participant Eng as On-call engineer
    participant Portal as Azure Portal / CLI
    participant SQLMI as SQL MI<br/>auto-failover group
    participant SB as Service Bus<br/>Geo-DR alias
    participant ASR as Azure Site Recovery<br/>(Citrix/CareLink PM VM tier)
    participant App as Secondary region<br/>app tier
    participant TM as Traffic Manager /<br/>Front Door

    Note over Mon,Eng: T+0 -- primary region outage detected
    Mon->>Eng: page: primary region unreachable
    Eng->>Eng: confirm outage, declare disaster<br/>per documented runbook -- T+15 min

    Note over Eng,SQLMI: Step 1 -- database (manual-initiated, per ADR-004)
    Eng->>Portal: trigger SQL MI failover group failover
    Portal->>SQLMI: promote secondary replica to primary
    activate SQLMI
    SQLMI-->>Portal: promotion complete -- T+30 min
    deactivate SQLMI

    Note over Eng,ASR: Step 2 -- compute (parallel with app validation)
    Eng->>Portal: trigger Azure Site Recovery failover
    Portal->>ASR: fail over Citrix / CareLink PM VMs
    activate ASR
    ASR->>App: boot VMs in secondary region,<br/>attach replicated disks
    ASR-->>Portal: failover complete -- T+90 min
    deactivate ASR

    Note over Eng,SB: Step 2b -- messaging (parallel with Step 2)
    Eng->>Portal: trigger Service Bus Geo-DR alias failover
    Portal->>SB: repoint alias to secondary namespace<br/>(topology only -- queues/topics/subscriptions/rules)
    SB-->>Portal: alias failover complete -- T+90 min
    Note right of SB: Gap (see ADR-011): Geo-DR replicates namespace<br/>topology, not in-flight message content.<br/>Messages mid-transit at failure time are not<br/>carried over automatically.

    Note over Eng,App: Step 3 -- validate before cutover
    Eng->>App: run smoke tests (auth, DB read/write,<br/>Service Bus connectivity to secondary alias)
    App-->>Eng: healthy -- T+150 min
    Eng->>Eng: initiate source-system reconciliation for the<br/>failover window -- LabCorp/Quest/Surescripts<br/>re-query for results/messages sent during the gap<br/>(does not block traffic cutover in Step 4)

    Note over Eng,TM: Step 4 -- traffic cutover
    Eng->>Portal: re-point Traffic Manager / Front Door<br/>to secondary region endpoint
    Portal->>TM: update routing
    TM-->>Eng: DNS propagated (TTL-bound) -- T+180 min

    Note over Mon,TM: RTO budget: 180 min actual vs. <= 240 min (4h) target<br/>RPO: bounded by SQL MI async replication interval, <= 15 min
